From 1000000000000000000000000000000000000456 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:01:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: bind Gemini P30E admission configuration

The production P30E diagnostic adds its wire option to the exact ordered
configuration inputs, changing their package-derived identity from
5968c24f... to 1e7f3047....  The runtime provenance leaf already carries
the latter identity, but the MT6797 production profile still expects the
former and therefore withholds READY at proof mask 0x40000.

Bind the production profile to the exact P30E configuration inputs.  Keep
the separate fixture identity unchanged and add no CPU request, power,
retry, CPU_OFF, storage, or device action.
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c
index 1cd32ee..24a572d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/mt6797_psci.c
@@ -63,8 +63,8 @@ static const u64 mt6797_a72_config_input_identity[ARM64_LATE_CPU_ID_WORDS] __ini
 };
 #else
 static const u64 mt6797_a72_config_input_identity[ARM64_LATE_CPU_ID_WORDS] __initconst = {
-	0x5968c24f1904c055, 0x9dea25480c41fbc7,
-	0xdb49e822dc3600d1, 0xbdd7632330853f40,
+	0x1e7f3047cd225aba, 0xca31d37bee725df5,
+	0x0cd0f310ff79edc5, 0x1b5838f03231b75b,
 };
 #endif
 
